.TH GETPRIORITY 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getpriority \- gets the lowest nice value among matching processes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/resource.h>
.B int getpriority(int which, unsigned int who);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gets the lowest nice value among matching processes. A successful result can be -1; clear errno before the call to distinguish an error. Linux priorities are per-thread.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the nice value, or \-1 with errno set. A successful nice value may also be \-1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getpriority (2)
